WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.629
The morning after the funeral Aunt Polly's kisses stopped.

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.438
At breakfast she was angry.

3
00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:12.019
"Tom Sawyer, I cannot believe you were so hard-hearted.

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.863
You made me, and everyone else, suffer for almost a week.

5
00:00:15.864 --> 00:00:19.669
You paddled on a log to come to your funeral.

6
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.256
You could have at least come home and let me know that you weren't dead."

7
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:24.914
Tom looked away.

8
00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:30.338
He knew that his aunt had suffered because of him, and his conscience wouldn't allow him to forget it.

9
00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:34.089
"You should have let me know," continued Aunt Polly.

10
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.263
Tom was sure that his guilty conscience was showing.

11
00:00:37.264 --> 00:00:42.030
"Tell me, Tom, that you would have come if you had thought of it."

12
00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:48.123
"I . . . ah . . . well . . . I don't know," stammered Tom.

13
00:00:48.124 --> 00:00:50.520
"It would have spoiled everything."

14
00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:54.492
"Oh, Tom, you break my heart," said Aunt Polly.

15
00:00:54.493 --> 00:00:57.363
"If you loved me, you would have come home.

16
00:00:57.364 --> 00:01:00.938
But all you care about are your ruined plans."

17
00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:04.346
Tom's conscience was paining him greatly.

18
00:01:04.347 --> 00:01:08.271
"You know, Auntie, I care for you."

19
00:01:08.272 --> 00:01:13.105
"I'd know better if you acted more like it," answered his aunt in a hurt tone.

20
00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.956
"I did wrong," confessed Tom.

21
00:01:15.957 --> 00:01:21.372
"I should have thought of you. In any case I did dream of you."

22
00:01:21.373 --> 00:01:26.633
"That isn't much," said Aunt Polly sadly. "But what did you dream about?"

23
00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:31.904
"It was Wednesday night, and I dreamed that you and Joe's mother were sitting here."

24
00:01:31.905 --> 00:01:37.687
"Why, she was here!" exclaimed Aunt Polly. "What else did you dream about?"

25
00:01:37.688 --> 00:01:44.245
"Oh, lots of stuff," said Tom. "But it's all kind of hazy."

26
00:01:44.246 --> 00:01:48.275
"Do try to remember," urged Aunt Polly.

27
00:01:48.276 --> 00:01:51.801
"Well, there was the wind, it blew . . ."

28
00:01:51.802 --> 00:01:54.796
"Yes," said Aunt Polly excitedly.

29
00:01:54.797 --> 00:01:58.473
"The wind did blow something. What did it blow?"

30
00:01:58.474 --> 00:02:03.829
Tom pressed his fingers to his forehead and said, "It blew the candle."

31
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:09.244
"Mercy!" exclaimed Aunt Polly. "That's right. Go on."

32
00:02:09.245 --> 00:02:12.527
"It's all coming back to me now," cried Tom.

33
00:02:12.528 --> 00:02:17.046
"You said I wasn't bad, and then you started to cry."

34
00:02:17.047 --> 00:02:19.929
"I did," said Aunt Polly.

35
00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:25.660
"Sereny Harper is going to hear about this before I'm an hour older. Go on."

36
00:02:25.661 --> 00:02:32.104
"Then Joe's mother started crying," Tom continued, "and she said Joe wasn't bad either.

37
00:02:32.105 --> 00:02:38.923
She also wished she hadn't punished Joe for taking the cream when she was the one who had thrown it out."

38
00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:44.486
"Tom," cried Aunt Polly, "you were dreaming like a prophet."

39
00:02:44.487 --> 00:02:46.916
Tom told his aunt everything.

40
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:50.739
He didn't leave out a thing, and Aunt Polly was in awe.

41
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:56.020
Finally Tom said, "I think you prayed for me. I was sorry.

42
00:02:56.021 --> 00:02:58.781
So I wrote a note saying we weren't dead.

43
00:02:58.782 --> 00:03:02.641
I put it on your table, and then I kissed you."

44
00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:09.484
"I know it's only a dream, but I can forgive you now," said Aunt Polly, hugging Tom.

45
00:03:09.485 --> 00:03:15.139
Sid thought the dream sounded too perfect to be a dream, but he kept his opinion to himself.

46
00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:20.093
When Tom was at school, Aunt Polly went to tell Joe's mother about the dream.

47
00:03:20.094 --> 00:03:23.891
At lunch Tom came home to a very angry aunt.

48
00:03:23.892 --> 00:03:27.341
"I should skin you alive," she said.

49
00:03:27.342 --> 00:03:30.548
"I ran over to Sereny Harper like an old fool.

50
00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:33.766
I told her about your amazing dream.

51
00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:38.263
She told me that Joe had told her you were here that night.

52
00:03:38.264 --> 00:03:40.399
It wasn't a dream at all!"

53
00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.942
Tom truly felt sorry for his joke.

54
00:03:42.943 --> 00:03:48.835
It had seemed like a good idea at breakfast, but now it just seemed mean.

55
00:03:48.836 --> 00:03:51.728
"You let me make a fool of myself.

56
00:03:51.729 --> 00:03:57.330
What kind of boy are you?" asked Aunt Polly. Tom hung his head in shame.

57
00:03:57.331 --> 00:03:59.768
"Why did you come over that night?

58
00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:04.198
Did you come to laugh at our troubles?" she demanded.

59
00:04:04.199 --> 00:04:08.626
"No," said Tom. "I came to tell you not to worry.

60
00:04:08.627 --> 00:04:11.306
I even wrote a note on a piece of bark.

61
00:04:11.307 --> 00:04:15.938
When I got the idea about the funeral, I put the note back in my pocket.

62
00:04:15.939 --> 00:04:21.159
But I did kiss you good-night." The hard lines on his aunt's face melted.

63
00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:26.627
The emotion in Tom's voice sounded too real for this to be a lie.

64
00:04:26.628 --> 00:04:31.796
After Tom returned to school, Aunt Polly wanted to see if she could find the piece of bark.

65
00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:37.152
She wondered if Tom really did write a note, or if this was just another one of his stories.

66
00:04:37.153 --> 00:04:43.542
Aunt Polly couldn't decide what to do, so she stood for several minutes, debating with herself.

67
00:04:43.543 --> 00:04:46.461
Curiosity finally got the better of her.

68
00:04:46.462 --> 00:04:49.497
She went into Tom's room and looked around.

69
00:04:49.498 --> 00:04:54.187
Lying on the floor was the piece of bark, and on the back was Tom's note.

70
00:04:54.188 --> 00:04:57.971
As Aunt Polly read it, tears came to her eyes.

71
00:04:57.972 --> 00:05:07.556
"Now I can forgive Tom, even though he has committed a million sins," she murmured.

